{
  "requirement": "Validation MUST report a requirement or example with a missing closing fence or an empty body. Full names of `{req}` and `{example}` definitions MUST be unique across requirements, examples, and named definitions. Habeas MUST report every duplicate full name, including collisions involving named definitions, and identify both the duplicate declaration and the first declaration.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gaps. The three obligations are implemented in `collect_definitions` and each has a test.\n\n**Code.** `collect_definitions` in `src/evidence.rs` (lines 414–571) carries all three obligations. It has an `{impl}` reference to `requirements.ci.definition_errors`. `load_definitions` (lines 149–166), which also has an `{impl}` reference, turns the collected errors into an aborting failure.\n\n1. **Missing closing fence.** When `!block.closed`, it pushes `\"{source}: {kind} {name} is missing a closing colon fence\"`. This applies to requirements, examples and definitions alike.\n2. **Empty body.** When the trimmed text is empty, it pushes `\"{source}: {kind} {name} has no text\"`.\n3. **Unique full names.** Declarations go into one `definitions` map shared by requirements, examples and named definitions.\n   - A name that is already present hits `Entry::Occupied` and pushes `\"{source}: duplicate {kind} {name}; first declared at {previous.source}\"`.\n   - Every later duplicate is reported, because the first declaration stays in the map.\n   - The message identifies both the duplicate (`source`) and the first declaration (`previous.get().source`).\n\n`definition_blocks` in `src/lib.rs` only computes the `closed` flag, a value its caller uses to report the error. Under the rules that does not count as implementing this requirement, so its lack of an `{impl}` reference here is not a gap.\n\n**Tests.**\n- Missing fence:\n  - `reports_a_missing_closing_colon_fence` (`src/evidence.rs`) tests an unclosed requirement.\n  - `example_errors_include_duplicates_invalid_bodies_and_missing_tests` tests an unclosed example.\n  - `discovery_errors_fail_before_configuration_or_inference` (`tests/authoring_batch.rs`) checks the same error through the `author` command.\n- Empty body:\n  - `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` asserts `requirement requirements.empty has no text`.\n  - `example_errors_include_duplicates_invalid_bodies_and_missing_tests` asserts `example rules.empty has no text`.\n- Duplicates:\n  - `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` covers a requirement that duplicates a requirement, with the first-declaration location.\n  - `example_errors_include_duplicates_invalid_bodies_and_missing_tests` covers requirement/requirement, example/requirement and example/example collisions.\n  - `duplicates_involving_named_definitions_name_the_first_declaration` (`tests/definitions.rs`) covers requirement→definition and definition→example collisions, asserting both locations.\n\nEach test carries a `{test}` reference to `requirements.ci.definition_errors`, and no `{fixme}` applies.",
  "references": "6cd1a20264fe9db14fcbb1b0ee38c4df338aff9d7de649d74d41f10da52a8f8e",
